{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00457",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.9,
      "end_seconds": 4.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Well, good evening, doctor, thank you for staying late."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.5,
      "end_seconds": 10.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "Yes, come in, take a seat. What can I do for you today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.54,
      "end_seconds": 26.9,
      "duration_seconds": 15.36,
      "text": "Right, you know, mainly blood on the toilet paper. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one. I've never really been one for hospitals. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.38,
      "end_seconds": 31.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Is this recent, or has it been a while?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.94,
      "end_seconds": 35.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "It's been like this since this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.63,
      "end_seconds": 43.67,
      "duration_seconds": 7.04,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.28,
      "end_seconds": 50.63,
      "duration_seconds": 6.35,
      "text": "Maybe a six out of ten on a bad day. It's worse with hard stools."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.99,
      "end_seconds": 53.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Does it come along with anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.16,
      "end_seconds": 62.54,
      "duration_seconds": 7.38,
      "text": "Constipation goes along with it, um, most of the time. The constipation? That's been for three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.7,
      "end_seconds": 67.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.88,
      "end_seconds": 71.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "So, thank you, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.31,
      "end_seconds": 76.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Any weight loss, fever or family history of bowel cancer?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.77,
      "end_seconds": 80.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Nothing like that, uh, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.17,
      "end_seconds": 87.99,
      "duration_seconds": 5.82,
      "text": "Okay, moving on to your background, any past medical history? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.49,
      "end_seconds": 96.0,
      "duration_seconds": 6.51,
      "text": "So, yes, low haemoglobin. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.4,
      "end_seconds": 109.0,
      "duration_seconds": 12.6,
      "text": "Just so you know how the rest of the visit will go: I'll finish my notes, we'll agree on the plan, and the front desk will help with anything that needs booking. You shouldn't need to chase anything yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.43,
      "end_seconds": 115.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "Oh, um, good, I was wondering how this would go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.52,
      "end_seconds": 119.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "What medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.21,
      "end_seconds": 126.65,
      "duration_seconds": 6.44,
      "text": "I mean, I'm on iron tablets, once a day for my blood count."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.7,
      "end_seconds": 134.08,
      "duration_seconds": 6.38,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.66,
      "end_seconds": 139.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Sulfa drugs. I come out in... well, a rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.97,
      "end_seconds": 142.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.07,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.56,
      "end_seconds": 146.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "I smoke, yes, around five a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.48,
      "end_seconds": 153.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.87,
      "text": "Alright, is there anyone at home who can help you out if you need it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.47,
      "end_seconds": 163.85,
      "duration_seconds": 9.38,
      "text": "Yes, there's family around most evenings, and they've been very good about checking in, although they do worry more than they need to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.97,
      "end_seconds": 167.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Let's get your blood pressure and the other basics."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.6,
      "end_seconds": 182.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "Hold still for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.38,
      "end_seconds": 204.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Okay: pressure 108 over 78, pulse 81, oxygen saturation is 98 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.65,
      "end_seconds": 207.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.01,
      "end_seconds": 211.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.43,
      "end_seconds": 217.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 218.88,
      "end_seconds": 219.58,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.47,
      "end_seconds": 222.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Can you lie back for me?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.81,
      "end_seconds": 235.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "There's a small external pile at the edge, and I don't see any fissure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.54,
      "end_seconds": 250.18,
      "duration_seconds": 11.64,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. From what you've told me and what I found, I think we're dealing with haemorrhoids at this stage. It could also be an anal fissure, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 250.88,
      "end_seconds": 253.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Is it something serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.99,
      "end_seconds": 269.27,
      "duration_seconds": 15.28,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like haemorrhoids, but I'd like to confirm. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had blood on the toilet paper, since this morning, and no family history of bowel cancer or weight loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 269.72,
      "end_seconds": 271.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.8,
      "end_seconds": 282.82,
      "duration_seconds": 10.02,
      "text": "I'm going to order blood tests, for rectal bleeding. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. I'm going to order a colonoscopy, for rectal bleeding."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 283.38,
      "end_seconds": 286.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Oh, alright. When can I do that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.27,
      "end_seconds": 298.11,
      "duration_seconds": 10.84,
      "text": "Let's use a soothing cream, twice a day, for one week. That's for haemorrhoids. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 300.95,
      "end_seconds": 302.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "Right, I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.13,
      "end_seconds": 324.81,
      "duration_seconds": 21.68,
      "text": "Soak in a warm bath for ten minutes after you pass stool, and don't strain. Make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids, two to three litres a day if you can, and get proper rest. Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.15,
      "end_seconds": 335.44,
      "duration_seconds": 10.29,
      "text": "I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if you pass a lot of blood or feel faint. Let's review you in three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 335.9,
      "end_seconds": 340.94,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "So, sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.49,
      "end_seconds": 347.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "Tell me what you've taken from all that, so I can fill in any gaps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 348.52,
      "end_seconds": 352.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "So, I come back in three weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.38,
      "end_seconds": 359.45,
      "duration_seconds": 6.07,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Right, that's all I have. Is there anything you wanted to ask?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 360.2,
      "end_seconds": 364.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "No, uh, you've explained it well. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 365.53,
      "end_seconds": 366.52,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "See you then."
    }
  ]
}